WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.820
From the franchise's animated beginnings through
2018's prequel installment and soft reboot

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.759
Bumblebee, get ready to relive all the highs
and lows of one of Hollywood's most successful

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:11.720
film series.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.200
Let's see how all the theatrically released
Transformers movies stack up against each

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:16.700
other.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.960
Transformers: The Last Knight is a troubling
movie.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:24.100
Sure, there are scattered flashes of brilliance,
like the scene when Megatron negotiates the

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.340
release of his crewmates, which does a great
job of showing the unique personalities of

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:29.140
the characters.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.120
It also has a cohesive tone that cleverly
leans on the humorous absurdity of transforming

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.899
robots interacting with humans, and features
some really striking, dynamic camera shots

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:41.399
that make every moment visually engaging.

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:46.149
However, the film's good scenes are vastly
outnumbered by bad ones, thanks to its bizarre

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:50.440
storyline, which entangles the history of
the Transformers with the Knights of the Round

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:50.940
Table.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.760
This central cog of the plot doesn't make
a lick of sense and retroactively undoes things

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.079
we've seen in the previous four movies, showing
the writers couldn't care less about the series'

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.520
story up to this point.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.560
And those aren't the only quality control
issues in the film.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.740
There are actual shots that made it into the
final cut that have cameramen in them.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.570
The aspect ratio constantly changes because
no one bothered to consider that a constantly

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.780
changing border might be distracting to viewers.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:21.520
Some central characters are completely useless,
and major plot points are consistently underdeveloped

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:25.960
and lazily executed, like Bumblebee's and
Optimus' climactic face-off.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.840
In short, most of The Last Knight represents
a sloppily produced missed opportunity.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:37.520
Transformers: Age of Extinction's human characters
all lack compelling motivation and have personalities

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.340
that range from infuriatingly annoying to
painfully cringeworthy.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:46.340
And the insufferable humans get the lion's
share of screen time because, besides Optimus

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:49.480
and Bumblebee, no Transformer gets a real
spotlight.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.220
Take the dinobots, for example.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.820
This movie promoted the heck out of them,
and yet they're only in the final 30 minutes

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:59.250
of the film, and even then, only in a few
big shots.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.340
The plot is another problem, since it undoes
much of the story that the previous three

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.200
Transformers movies established.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:09.900
It's not done in a crafty way, either, the
movie just presents its retroactive changes

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:13.320
to the series' continuity and pretends no
one will notice.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.260
This movie really puts the "stink" in "extinction."

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.680
Transformers: Revenge of the Fallen is a tricky
one.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.180
Although critics absolutely blasted it, fans
remain divided.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:29.220
On one hand, it has the allure of Megan Fox's
Mikaela Banes and goofball charm of Shia LaBeouf's

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:29.720
Sam Witwicky.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:35.180
It also features a lot of top-tier CGI action
and epic fights, such as the forest battle

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.480
when Optimus Prime dies defending against
multiple Decepticons.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:43.220
Plus, as is guaranteed with any Michael Bay
film, the cinematography is as stylish and

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:45.430
stereotypically "Hollywood" as it gets.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:51.000
For fans of pretty actors, likable enough
characters, gorgeous cinematography, and mind-numbingly

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.500
bombastic action, there's a lot to love in
Revenge of the Fallen.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.700
However, this movie is also loaded with a
lot of not-so-great elements.

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:03.650
The plot contradicts itself constantly, some
of the characters, both human and robot, are

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:08.370
pretty obnoxious, there's a lot of crude and
unnecessary humor, and the tone oscillates

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:13.930
between serious action-drama and juvenile
comedy too clumsily for anything to be taken

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.680
seriously, or humorously.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.680
Blame the farting airplane-robot.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:29.840
With that in mind, if you just want some incredible
CGI action featuring transforming robots,

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:35.320
both of the farting and non-farting variety,
Revenge of the Fallen can still be a fun time.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.560
Though it fails to hold up by today's standards
for animated sci-fi flicks, when observed

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:46.180
as a relic of 1986 and an ode to the Transformers
toys, Transformers: The Movie does a solid

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:46.680
job.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:52.180
Beyond its fan-pleasing, ultra-expansive cast
of transforming robots, it has other merits,

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:52.980
such as its plot.

00:03:53.409 --> 00:03:57.760
This movie's story goes to some very Game
of Thrones-like places in a way that's wholly

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.730
befitting of the Transformers' perpetual civil
war.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:04.880
Though some might find it to be a bit dark,
a lot of fans really love that this is the

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:09.769
one Transformers movie that dared to take
risks with its plot beats, putting beloved

00:04:09.769 --> 00:04:14.320
Transformers' lives on the line to keep stakes
high and maintain the realism of war.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.460
For all these pros, there's no getting around
the fact that the movie has issues.

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:23.300
Its animation quality is often weak, the soundtrack
is infused with too much cheesy rock for its

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:28.500
own good, and the plot fails to articulate
certain points in smart, digestible ways.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.000
Still, the movie is a solid '86 Transformers
time capsule.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:37.240
It's got a great voice cast, cool robots,
it explores surprisingly risky themes, overall,

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:41.840
it sports many or most of the key ingredients
that helped get the Transformers franchise

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.880
where it is today.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:48.020
Transformers: Dark of the Moon marked the
first time the franchise really dug deep into

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:52.970
historical revisionism for plot points, and
it remains the only time it's panned out well.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:57.950
The plot uses moon landing conspiracy theories
to its advantage and weaves them into Transformers

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:02.750
lore in a way that's both smart and compelling,
giving characters from the previous two movies

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:06.980
new information that organically feeds into
new missions and character arcs.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:12.300
Plus, the finale is basically just one hour
of breathtaking, uninterrupted robot carnage,

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:16.930
for those who only care about seeing Optimus
fly a jetpack, swing a sword, and stab robots

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:17.700
left and right.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:23.260
Dark of the Moon hits all of Michael Bay's
usual beats: pretty stars, hot cars, incredible

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:27.860
camerawork, breathtaking scope, insane action,
and lots of explosions.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:32.810
But this movie, unlike some of Bay's others,
backs all of those things up with real heart,

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.030
real characters, and real storytelling.

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.620
Plus, the CGI is outstanding and the soundtrack
is killer.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.840
Many casual moviegoers and film critics would
agree that Michael Bay's first foray into

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.360
the Transformers universe remains his best.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:52.340
2007's Transformers is a narratively tight
movie that keeps its action, plot, and characters

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:56.860
all firmly planted within our reality, though
it also leans heavily on the humorous nature

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:58.580
of its central sci-fi premise.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:04.440
In this sense, it's almost a Marvel movie:
fun, minimal on melodrama, loaded with quirky,

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:09.520
likable characters that operate within a believable
yet fantastical universe, and inoffensive.

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.360
Well, relatively inoffensive:

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:17.140
"Hey hey!"

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.340
"Bumblebee, stop lubricating the man."

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:25.720
Back in 2007, Transformers set a new bar for
creativity and polish in Hollywood visual

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:29.780
effects, which remains one of this movie's
biggest merits and a key part of why it's

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.040
remembered so fondly.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:35.640
But it's also beloved for being the starting
point of an engaging trilogy centered around

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:40.500
Shia LaBeouf, Optimus Prime, and Bumblebee
getting into wacky adventures together, with

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:45.069
Shia as the relatable stand-in for every kid
who's always wanted to meet a Transformer

00:06:45.069 --> 00:06:45.920
in real life.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:51.100
For many people, Bumblebee is likely to be
the most pleasing Transformers movie to date.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:55.010
Though the Michael Bay movies attempted to
make everything as cool as possible, Bumblebee

00:06:55.010 --> 00:07:00.979
takes a step back and focuses almost exclusively
on injecting relatable emotion into the performance

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:03.720
and arc of its titular robot and lead cast.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:08.620
Spectacle is secondary in Bumblebee, and though
that's going to require a substantial gear-shift

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:13.540
for fans of the previous films to fully appreciate,
it's an interesting breath of fresh air for

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.200
the franchise.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:19.120
Director Travis Knight's style revolves around
sensitivity and nuance, and he handles the

00:07:19.139 --> 00:07:24.289
film's social and interpersonal dynamics with
a delicacy and care rarely seen in Hollywood

00:07:24.289 --> 00:07:25.080
blockbusters.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:30.000
That alone makes this a more easily digestible
film than most of the other Transformers flicks.

00:07:30.009 --> 00:07:34.520
That's why Bumblebee reigns supreme over its
competition: it may not indulge in the pure

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:39.069
over-the-top action of the Bay-helmed installments,
but it's definitely a bit more innocent, as

00:07:39.069 --> 00:07:40.580
well as a good deal more human.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.840
"God I'm so screwed."

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:48.680
And for a viewing audience that's entirely
human, it turns out those qualities really

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:49.180
matter.

